Package: parvenu
Title: Multithreaded Base R Functions and Text Search for Large Vectors
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R: person("Lukas", "Jung", , "jung-lukas@gmx.net", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Multithreaded functions for large vectors, written in Rust,
    in two families. Versions of match(), %in%, duplicated(), unique(),
    anyDuplicated(), union(), intersect(), setdiff(), factor(), table(),
    findInterval(), as.Date(), as.POSIXct(), rank(), rowsum(), and
    approx() give the same results as base R, and fall back to it below
    the size where threads pay off; rows can also be matched on several
    key columns at once. Text search detects, counts, locates, extracts,
    and replaces regex matches, in the syntax of Rust's regex crate, and
    looks up many literal terms or regexes at once: which of them each
    string contains, how many hits it has, or replacing them all, in one
    pass per string.
